{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaC_not_const_mul_additive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaC_not_const_mul_additive","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation.lean#L114-L124","doc":"**The exclusion, convention C.**  Same statement in the square-root\nvariable, where `q ↦ q²` is `u ↦ u²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaD_not_const_mul_additive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaD_not_const_mul_additive","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation.lean#L101-L112","doc":"**The exclusion, convention D.**  For no constant `c` and no additive `L`\nis `α_D` equal to `c · L` — in particular `α_D ≠ c · ln`, so `α_D` is not a\nconstant-residue Kohno–Drinfeld holonomy angle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaC_fails_doubling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaC_fails_doubling","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation.lean#L95-L99","doc":"**`α_C` fails the doubling identity at `u = 2`**: `α_C(2·2) = −195/32`\nwhile `2·α_C(2) = −9/4 = −72/32`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaC_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaC_four","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation.lean#L91-L93","doc":"`α_C (4) = −195/32`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaC_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaC_two","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation.lean#L87-L89","doc":"`α_C (2) = −9/8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaD_fails_doubling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaD_fails_doubling","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation.lean#L81-L85","doc":"**`α_D` fails the doubling identity at `q = 2`**: `α_D(2·2) = 705/136`\nwhile `2·α_D(2) = 9/10`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaD_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaD_four","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation.lean#L77-L79","doc":"`α_D (4) = 705/136`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaD_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaD_two","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation.lean#L73-L75","doc":"`α_D (2) = 9/20`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaC","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation.lean#L67-L71","doc":"The ladder phase under **convention C**, in the square-root variable\n`u = √q`: `z_C = u/(u²+1)` and `h = u² − u⁻²`.  Writing it in `u` keeps the\nstatement algebraic; `q ↦ q²` corresponds to `u ↦ u²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.alphaD","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation.lean#L62-L65","doc":"The ladder phase under **convention D**, `α_D = (z_D − 1)·h/2` with\n`z_D = q³/(q²+1)` and `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.const_mul_additive_doubles","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.LogFunEq.const_mul_additive_doubles","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/PhaseFailsLogFunctionalEquation.lean#L49-L60","doc":"**Any constant multiple of an additive function satisfies `f (q*q) = 2 f q`.**\n\n`ln` is the case at hand (`ln (q²) = 2 ln q`), and a constant-residue\nKohno–Drinfeld holonomy angle is `c · ln q`.  The hypothesis is only additivity\non the diagonal, so the lemma applies to any logarithm-like scale, and `c` is\narbitrary — which is what makes the exclusion below hold for *every* `c` at\nonce. ","signatureChunk":0}]}